1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,560
The third habit is detachment from outcomes.
第三个习惯，是不过分执着于结果。

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:09,440
One consistent habit I've noticed among highly achieving women who are also happy and content and feeling in control of their lives.
我注意到，那些成就很高、同时快乐满足、觉得生活由自己掌握的女性，有一个共同习惯。

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:14,639
Is that they measure success by effort alignment and input not by things outside their control.
她们用努力、行动与目标是否一致，以及投入来衡量成功，而不是用自己控制不了的事情。

4
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:19,919
A good way of thinking about this is separating out goals into input goals versus output goals.
一个理解方式，是把目标区分为投入目标和产出目标。

5
00:00:19,919 --> 00:00:25,200
One way that I've developed to think about this over time is separating goals into almost three stages three categories.
我逐渐形成的一种思考方式，是把目标大致分成三个阶段、三种类别。

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,400
There's input goals there's output goals and there's outcome goals.
有投入目标、产出目标，还有结果目标。

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:34,160
An example with my youtube channel is an input goal is I want to spend 15 hours on my youtube channel every week.
拿我的 YouTube 频道来说，投入目标可以是：每周花十五个小时做频道。

8
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:37,359
An output goal is I want to post one video per week.
产出目标可以是：每周发布一个视频。

9
00:00:37,359 --> 00:00:42,320
An outcome goal is I want to gain x number of subscribers every month.
结果目标则是：每个月增加某个数量的订阅者。

10
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:48,720
And as you can see as we go from input to output to outcome I have much more control over the input versus the outcome.
你可以看到，从投入到产出再到结果，我对投入的控制远远高于对结果的控制。

11
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:54,470
It's essentially 100 within my control whether I actually spend 15 hours of work on my youtube channel.
我是否真的花十五个小时做频道，基本上完全由我自己掌握。

12
00:00:54,480 --> 00:01:01,270
Then for the output there's a little bit less control there because I don't necessarily know how much research a video will need until I really start.
至于产出，可控程度就低一点，因为真正开始前，我不一定知道一个视频需要做多少研究。

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:07,519
I'm not sure how long the editing process is going to take so the output is slightly less predictable than the input but it's still broadly under my control.
我也不确定剪辑需要多久，所以产出比投入略难预测，但大体上仍在我的控制范围内。

14
00:01:07,519 --> 00:01:13,440
And finally the outcome goals such as I want to hit 1 million subscribers in x amount of time that is the least in my control.
最后是结果目标，比如在某段时间内达到一百万订阅者；这一类最不由我掌控。

15
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:16,959
Because there's so much beyond my control that I cannot account for.
因为有太多超出我控制范围、无法全部考虑到的因素。

16
00:01:16,959 --> 00:01:23,110
And so whether or not I actually get there is partly to do with my inputs and the output but then it's also partly due to external conditions.
所以我最终能否做到，部分取决于我的投入和产出，也部分取决于外部条件。

17
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:27,919
So for me while for my youtube channel I do have an outcome goal for where I want to go with the channel.
对我来说，虽然我确实为频道未来的发展方向设了一个结果目标——

18
00:01:27,919 --> 00:01:33,520
And I think that's very helpful for setting a north star on the day to day I actually focus more on my input and output.
而且我觉得这很有助于确立方向，但在日常中，我实际更关注投入和产出。

19
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:38,799
Once I've set the outcome goal and I've used it to generate a northstar and a strategy I then let go of it.
设定结果目标、用它确定方向和策略后，我就放下对它的执着。

20
00:01:38,799 --> 00:01:40,400
I detach from it I take a step back.
我与它拉开一点距离，退一步看。

21
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:47,510
And actually that level of detachment allows me to work from a place of joy and progress rather than a place of stress and pressure.
这种距离感让我带着喜悦、着眼进步去工作，而不是带着压力和紧张。

22
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:54,880
This habit actually draws directly from principles of non attachment and equanimity which are core concepts in eastern philosophy.
她说，这个习惯直接借鉴了东方哲学中的不执着与平等心这两个核心概念。

23
00:01:54,880 --> 00:02:01,920
Psychological suffering arises when we cling to specific outcomes and identify our success or worth with these external results.
她认为，当我们紧抓特定结果，把成功或自身价值与外部结果等同起来时，就会产生心理痛苦。

24
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:09,120
The top 1 understand that attaching your happiness to these outcomes that you cannot fully control creates this opportunity for unnecessary suffering.
她说，顶尖人士明白：把幸福系在无法完全掌控的结果上，可能带来不必要的痛苦。

25
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:14,719
And so instead by focusing on what we can control our effort our intention our process rather than external validation.
因此，她主张把注意力放在能控制的努力、意图和过程上，而不是寻求外界认可——

26
00:02:14,719 --> 00:02:18,960
Or specific results you cultivate what eastern philosophers call wise effort.
也不是一心盯着具体结果；她把这称为培养东方哲学家所说的“明智的努力”。

27
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:23,040
And this mindset shift while it sounds like taking a step back from making goals.
这种心态转变虽然听起来像是从设定目标上退了一步——

28
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:28,960
Actually paradoxically improves performance by reducing the anxiety and pressure that often sabotage success.
她却认为，它能减少经常妨碍成功的焦虑和压力，从而反倒改善表现。

29
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:36,630
The practice involves training yourself to find satisfaction in the quality of your actions and inputs rather than the results or outcomes that they produce.
这个练习是训练自己：从行动和投入的质量中找到满足，而不是只从它们产生的结果中获得满足。

30
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:41,279
So for example instead of defining success as getting a 100 000 views on a youtube video.
比如，与其把成功定义成一个 YouTube 视频获得十万次观看——

31
00:02:41,279 --> 00:02:46,000
Maybe I could reframe it as creating content that genuinely serves my audience and that I'm proud of.
我也许可以换一种定义：做出真正对观众有帮助、也让我自豪的内容。

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,040
This detachment doesn't mean that I care any less it actually just means that I'm directing my energy more effectively.
不执着不代表我不在乎，只是我在更有效地使用精力。

33
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,839
And research in sports psychology actually confirms this approach.
她还说，运动心理学研究印证了这种做法。

34
00:02:53,839 --> 00:02:59,269
Athletes who focus on process over outcomes consistently outperform those who are fixated on winning.
她称，关注过程而非结果的运动员，表现始终优于一心只想取胜的人。

35
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:06,560
Because counterintuitively the mental freedom created by letting go of outcome attachment allows for more presence creativity and flow.
她认为，反直觉的是，放下对结果的执着带来的心理自由，会让人更专注当下、更有创造力，也更容易进入心流。

36
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:12,320
Which are all qualities that ultimately improve performance and are so important for leaders to embody.
她认为，这些品质最终有助于提升表现，也是领导者很需要展现出来的。
